+## Identity plane — sanctioned global access (2026-10)
+
+The identity tables (`users`, `sessions`) and the invite/identity KV records are
+resolved BEFORE a tenant context exists (login, registration, email verification,
+password reset, invite acceptance). Each `(file, table)` pair below is a
+deliberate, reviewed class-2 entry in `SANCTIONED_GLOBAL` (`scripts/forensic-sql-scan.sh`):
+
+| File | Table | Why it is global and safe |
+|---|---|---|
+| `auth_flows.rs` | `saas_runtime_records` | identity KV (`organization` by id, `user` / `membership` by lookup_key) resolved before a tenant context; org comes from the payload, membership writes are org-bound in the same transaction |
+| `auth_flows.rs` | `invites` | invite acceptance locates the row by a 256-bit token hash (or id inside the same transaction); `organization_id` is taken from the row, never chosen by the accepting user |
+| `auth_flows.rs` | `users` | registration: a user is a deployment-wide identity (one login may belong to several organizations) |
+| `postgres.rs` | `users` | durable identity persistence; membership is recorded separately and org-scoped |
+| `email_verification.rs` | `users` | lookup by normalised email; flag update by the user id taken from the verified single-use token |
+| `password_reset.rs` | `users` | quiet lookup by email (enumeration-safe); password update by the user id from the hashed single-use token |
+| `password_reset.rs` | `sessions` | a reset revokes ALL live sessions of the user across every organization (security requirement) |
+
+Scope limit: an entry covers every statement of that table in that file. A new
+org-unsafe statement added to one of these files would not be flagged by the
+scanner; code review must check new statements against this table.
+
